Run:      2026-10-15 18:52-19:01 NZDT (the DUT's clock reads UTC and runs 3 s behind
          the box's, measured by bracketing `show clock` between two box readings;
          device times quoted below are swi_d's own UTC)
Bench:    tb277, consoles u2 = swi_d (DUT); Test Engineer bidhanc@bidhanc-dl
Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     T43848 "IPv4_ARP - Proxy ARP". No authored step text exists for this case, in
          AWPTCM or in ck.db: an exact-title lookup found step text for one other case
          in this campaign and none for this one, so there are no authored steps and no
          authored expected results. The headings below say what was actually
          exercised. The case was graded against:
            - X960 platform support TPS row 23 "Proxy-ARP", priority 1, "Yes", note
              column empty;
            - the IP Feature Overview and Configuration Guide, Proxy ARP section;
            - the DUT's own CLI surface, read off by a read-only `?` probe (quoted in
              STEP 0): `ip proxy-arp` and `ip local-proxy-arp` are both INTERFACE
              commands and neither takes a sub-option.
          Objective: with `ip proxy-arp` on an interface, the DUT answers ARP requests
          arriving on that interface for addresses it can reach via a DIFFERENT
          interface, using its own MAC; it does not answer for addresses it cannot
          route, nor for addresses on the receiving interface's own subnet; the
          behaviour is per-interface; the answered address is genuinely reachable
          through the DUT; the command is removable; and it survives a reboot. 6 steps
          as executed, plus a baseline.
Build:    swi_d  sin_x96056-20261012-24  (flash:/x960-tb277.rel, build date Mon Oct 12 2026)
          AT-x960-56YSQ, S/N A2WQS700B, standalone, console u2 @115200
Configs:  swi_d.cfg (running-config after setup, before step 1; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- `ip proxy-arp` makes the DUT answer, with its own MAC, ARP requests
arriving on the configured interface for an address reachable through a different one;
it is gated on reachability, bounded away from the receiving interface's own subnet,
applied per-interface, and the answer leads to real delivery. Removal and reboot
persistence are both proven on the wire.
      default state ....................... OFF: no proxy line in running-config, and
                                            0 replies for the proxied target
      instrument control, every leg ....... the DUT's own address answered 3 of 3
      proxy answer ........................ 192.168.48.5 answered 3 of 3,
                                            is-at e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43, the DUT's own MAC
      held per-interface .................. the line sits under `interface vlan10`,
                                            not globally
      no route ............................ 10.99.99.99 answered 0 of 3, feature on
      same subnet as the ingress interface  192.168.10.78 answered 0 of 3, feature on
      per-interface, mirror direction ..... vlan48 silent for 192.168.10.5 until the
                                            same command is added there, then 3 of 3
      the proxied address is reachable .... 5 of 5 frames sent to the DUT's MAC emerged
                                            on vlan48 addressed to the real owner
      removal, both interfaces ............ running-config empty of proxy lines, both
                                            wires back to 0 replies, controls still 3
      reboot .............................. the whole four-target matrix reproduces
                                            frame for frame, negatives included
CAVEAT:  One `ip proxy-arp` interface pair on two untagged access VLANs, IPv4 only, on a
         standalone unit. The proxied address was reachable over a directly connected
         route; behaviour against a static or dynamic route to a further hop was not
         exercised. `ip local-proxy-arp` was not configured at any point here -- the
         same-subnet limb above measures what plain `ip proxy-arp` does with such a
         request, not what local proxy ARP would do with it.

